#--------------------------------------------------------------------
#  PRIMO Macro v1.0
#
#  Macro: PRIMOMacro_PENELOPE_Phantom
#  Purpose: Simulate segment s1 s2 and s3 to tally a dose distribution
#               in a water phantom
#  Requirements:
#    - An existing project with a linac set in an operational mode
#  Adjust to your requirements:
#   - beam parameters  {set to the default of the first nominal energy}
#   - simulation parameters {10^9 histories}
#
#  last update: March, 2018
#-------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1- Remove any ct, plan and structures in the project
#     by creating a water phantom w/ default dimensions and 30 cm depth
phantom \mats=water \thicks=30.0

# 2- Set the beam to the default values of the first nominal energy
config.beam \nominal=1 

# 3- Configure field 1. Isocenter on the center of the phantom surface
#     size=10x10cm2, no rotations.
#    
config.field \rotations=0,0,0 \iso=0,0,0 jaws=5,5,5,5

# 4- Set the simulation params for segment s1 + s2 + s3
config.simu  \seg=s1s2s3 \engine=penelope \histories=1000000000 \seeds \cpus=4

# 5- Variance reduction = splitting roulette (radius for a 40x40 cm2 field) + 
#     splitting = 50 on s3
config.vr \roulettefull \split=50

# 6- Do simulate with penelope
simulate

# end-of-macro -----------------------------------------------------


